WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.648 --> 00:00:11.725
Sign in as the business owner.

2
00:00:11.825 --> 00:00:16.916
Open Reports, then Sales Report. It lists every sale in the period you choose.

3
00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:23.537
The cards on top give the totals: revenue, number of sales, average sale value, refunds and net revenue.

4
00:00:23.637 --> 00:00:28.509
Below them is each sale with its customer, items, discount, tax and total.

5
00:00:29.346 --> 00:00:35.206
Use the shortcuts to pick a period quickly. Last 7 days narrows the report to the past week.

6
00:00:36.508 --> 00:00:41.112
Or enter your own From and To dates, then click Apply.

7
00:00:42.415 --> 00:00:48.001
The Branch filter shows one branch only. Choose Camp and apply to see just that branch.

8
00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:56.506
The Payments Report shows how customers paid: the total collected and a split by method, such as card and cash.

9
00:00:57.807 --> 00:01:02.625
Use it to check the till and the bank against what you expect to receive.

10
00:01:02.725 --> 00:01:08.972
The Profit Report compares revenue with the cost of goods sold, so you see gross profit and margin.

11
00:01:09.073 --> 00:01:13.172
Last 30 days gives a good picture of how the month is going.

12
00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:19.300
Revenue minus cost of goods gives gross profit. The table shows the same figures for each sale.

13
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:25.534
The Inventory Report values your stock: stock value, SKU count, low stock and out of stock items.

14
00:01:27.135 --> 00:01:31.951
It lists each product per branch with its quantity, cost price and value.

15
00:01:32.974 --> 00:01:39.441
Every report has an Export CSV button. Click it to download the figures and open them in a spreadsheet.

16
00:01:39.541 --> 00:01:46.392
That is the reporting set. Pick a period, pick a branch, read the totals, export when you need them elsewhere.
